The original reads `mesg->numFields` and `mesg->fields` through the `mesg` pointer on every iteration. This version loads both into locals once and then walks the fields with a pointer. The lookup order, the returned index and the `FIT_UINT16_INVALID` returns are all unchanged.

The gain is likely small, because the time is probably dominated by `GetMesg`, which this function can't safely change.

```cpp
const FIT_UINT16 Profile::GetFieldIndex(const FIT_UINT16 mesgNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    const MESG *mesg = GetMesg(mesgNum);

    if (mesg == NULL)
        return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;

    const FIT_UINT16 n = mesg->numFields;
    const auto *fields = mesg->fields;

    for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (fields[i].num == fieldNum)
            return i;
    }

    return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;
}
```